{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>and singers, in you</b> — opposite the man of Elohim. And there are singers and dancers who do not cease, like spring waters; and \"these my eyes\" is like \"upon all the choice ones of my hands.\" And the way of the world is that the singers are fewer than the dancers. And \"singers of Zion\" is like \"the dancers,\" and the form of חוללים is like אמרתי להוללים."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 87, :notes {0 "The comment is textually difficult: the phrase לנכח איש האלהים and the parsing of the analogies (מעייני מים / מעיני / על כל אצילי ידי from Num 8:10 and Isa 49:22 respectively, plus the Amos 6:5 and Psalms references) are compressed and possibly corrupt; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:17.794401061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}